<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theodore Svetoslav</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1322">1322</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a> · Also known as Todor Svetoslav</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theodore Svetoslav was tsar of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> from 1300 to 1322, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/george-i-terter">George I Terter</a>. Long a hostage of the Mongol warlord Nogai, he seized the throne after Nogai's fall and ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a>'s domination of Bulgaria. He defeated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantines</a> in 1304, recovered the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> ports and made peace with Andronikos II in 1307, giving the country a period of stability and prosperity.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/theodore-svetoslav.jpg" alt="Theodore Svetoslav" width="320" height="328" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Silver_coin_of_Theodore_Svetoslav.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
